    "name": {
      "value": "Fiend Warding Tattoo"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "som"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "Many cultures of Golarion have a tattoo to turn away harm; as such, warding tattoos often resemble whichever dangers are most common to the culture, such as a wild beast or a whirlpool in the high seas of the Shackles.\n\n- **Activate:** Reaction\n- **Frequency:** once per day\n- **Trigger:** An enemy, hazard, or the environment makes an attack against your AC, requires you to attempt a saving throw, or causes you to take damage automatically\n\nUntil the end of the current turn, against the triggering effect, you gain a +1 status bonus to AC and saving throws and gain resistance 2 to damage.\n\nYou gain resistance 2 to spells cast by fiends and magical attacks by fiends, which increases to 5 when the tattoo is activated."
    },
